  "body": "## What changed\n- Added the clean-room Siemens Sinumerik 810M post in `assets/posts/sinumerik-810m.cps` (`Siemens 810M`).\n- Added the EMCO VMC-200 machine profile in `assets/machines/emco-vmc-200.mch` (`EMCO VMC-200`).\n- Registered both in `crates/app/src/posting_files.rs` and updated cross-post suites in `crates/app/tests/conformance.rs`, `crates/app/tests/machine.rs`, and `crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs`.\n- Added pinning suites `crates/post/tests/sinumerik_810m_post.rs`, `crates/post/tests/script_sinumerik_810m.rs`, and `crates/app/tests/sinumerik_810m_post.rs`.\n- Added recorded goldens in `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/sinumerik-810m/` and `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sinumerik-810m/`.\n- Added an owner air-cut kit in `docs/tester-kits/sinumerik-810m-vmc200/` and decision notes in `docs/decisions/2888-sinumerik-810m.md`.\n- Review fix (`e4996c3cf6812760696a0f73b53194f4a8b86c55`): preserved active spindle direction (`spinRev`) until `endPreamble()`, initialized `R11=3` before every `L84` call, initialized `R16` and `R17` before `L85`, and initialized `R12=0` and `R13=0` before `L86`.\n\n## Cause\nThe existing Siemens post (`assets/posts/sinumerik.cps`) targets Sinumerik 840D (`%_N_..._MPF`, `;` comments, `G700`/`G710`, `G505`+, `CYCLE832`, and ISO G81-G89 blocks). Sinumerik 810M GA3 uses `%MPF1`-`%MPF9999`, parenthesized comments capped at 41 CRT chars, 120-char blocks, 4-digit `N9999` sequence numbers, `G71` geometry-only units (`F` stays metric), settable offsets `G54`-`G57` only, plain `G41`/`G42` without `NORM`, incremental `I`/`J`/`K` arcs, `G4 F` dwell, and `L81`-`L89` subroutine cycles with R-parameters (`R00`-`R17`).\n\n## Tests\nAll commands below ran on the final head `e4996c3cf6812760696a0f73b53194f4a8b86c55`:\n- Post pins (`cargo test -p camcraft-post --test sinumerik_810m_post`): 11 passed, 0 failed.\n- Recorded script suite (`cargo test -p camcraft-post --test script_sinumerik_810m`): 11 passed, 0 failed.\n- App conformance (`cargo test -p camcraft-app --test conformance`): 7 passed, 0 failed.\n- App catalog (`cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog`): 37 passed, 0 failed, 4 ignored (heavy lane).\n- App 810M suite (`cargo test -p camcraft-app --test sinumerik_810m_post`): 3 passed, 0 failed.\n- Pin proof (review fixes): each of the four new pins failed on the unfixed post and failed when its fix was reverted independently, then passed when restored:\n  - `cycles_preserve_forward_and_reverse_spindle_direction` (reverted `spinRev` reset to `startPreamble` -> RED; restored -> GREEN).\n  - `deep_to_tap_initializes_z_axis_before_every_l84` (removed `R11=3` from `L84` -> RED; restored -> GREEN).\n  - `ream_initializes_cutting_and_retraction_feeds` (removed `R16`/`R17` from `L85` -> RED; restored -> GREEN).\n  - `bore_initializes_lateral_retraction_offsets` (removed `R12=0`/`R13=0` from `L86` -> RED; restored -> GREEN).\n- Earlier guard mutation checks also verified red on removal and green on restore for `workOffsetMax = 4`, `programUnits = \"mm\"`, `safeZ`, `N9999`, and `L84` encoder dwell.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` against `e313aa663869561b2748b9a0c5dac295470c8667`): GREEN, 759 steps, 0 failed (77.6 min).\n- Clippy (`cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`): clean (exit 0).\n\n## Heavy lanes\n- Head: `e4996c3cf6812760696a0f73b53194f4a8b86c55`.\n- Base: `upstream/main` at `e313aa663869561b2748b9a0c5dac295470c8667`.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: GREEN, 204 steps, 0 failed (wall 44.6 min).\n- Lanes: all selected app heavy targets, including `lib`, `bins`, `doc`, and `app heavy: example_catalog` (ok in 12s).\n- Known failures #1950 and #2849 failed as expected and were accepted by the gate.\n\n## Goldens moved\n- Zero existing `.nc` or `.cl` goldens changed.\n- Added 11 new recorded outputs in `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/sinumerik-810m/`, 13 new conformance `.nc` files in `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sinumerik-810m/`, `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/synth_sinumerik-810m.nc`, and `docs/tester-kits/sinumerik-810m-vmc200/air_cut_vmc200.mpf`.\n- Review fix (`e4996c3cf6812760696a0f73b53194f4a8b86c55`) regenerated two of this PR's new 810M goldens with `WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p camcraft-app --test conformance`:\n  - `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sinumerik-810m/tap_plate.nc`: adds `R11=3` before `L84 P1`.\n  - `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/synth_sinumerik-810m.nc`: adds `R11=3` before `L84 P1` after `L83 P1` (`R11=1`).\n\n## Not exercised\n- Physical execution on an EMCO VMC-200 or Sinumerik 810M controller hardware (documented air-cut kit included for owner hardware read-back).\n- Optional post behaviors not present on base 810M: `G70` inch output (unsafe due to metric `F` feedrate), `FINEBORE`, probing, rotary/tilt axes, and `Control` WCS rotation.\n- UI changes: none (no UI files touched).\n\n## Overlaps\nOpen PRs `#2515`, `#2646`, `#2951`..`#2999`, `#3046`, and `#3294` append different post/machine entries to the shared tables in `crates/app/src/posting_files.rs`, `crates/app/tests/conformance.rs`, `crates/app/tests/machine.rs`, and `crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs`; none touch `sinumerik-810m.cps` or `emco-vmc-200.mch`. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Added Siemens Sinumerik 810M 3-axis milling post, EMCO VMC-200 machine profile, and owner air-cut kit.\nFixes #2888\n",
